<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/72/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/72/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/72/>;
    dc:modified '2019-12-19T17:24:19'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'queen scallop dredges'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Code deprecated on 20Dec2019: created in error. Description was: The dredges used to target queen scallops are wider and higher than a traditional scallop dredge. They do not have tooth bar across the front, instead they have either a metal grid, or tickler chains to get the scallops to lift up off the seabed and swim into the dredge. The scallops then fall back into a bag made of metal rings. Some fishermen are replacing the tickler chain and metal grid with a strip of rubber matting across the front of the dredge (source seafish.org).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L05::72'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/71/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/71/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/71/>;
    dc:modified '2019-12-19T17:12:49'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'scallop dredges'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Code deprecated on 20Dec2019: created in error. Description was: Rigid structures with a chain mail collecting bag, towed on the seabed to target king scallops. Generally used by towing several dredges side by side behind the vessel (source: seafish.org).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L05::71'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/391/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/391/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/391/>;
    dc:modified '2019-12-19T15:01:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sediment suction samplers'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Devices that collect samples from the sediment layer surface using suction. The mechanism of suction can be accomplished by either vacuum, by pressure difference between the air inside the sampler and surrounding water, by pumping water directly into the sampler or by under pressure air to elevate the sediment inside the sampler. Devices are typically diver- or remotely-operated.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L05::391'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/24/4/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/24/4/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/24/>;
    dc:modified '2019-12-19T11:32:58'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'benthos samplers'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A mechanical device that collects organisms from the seafloor. Includes dredges, sledges, weighted nets like beam trawls, and ROV manipulators.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L05::24'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/EMSR/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/EMSR/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/EMSR/>;
    dc:modified '2019-12-11T18:23:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'electromagnetic sensors'@en ;
    skos:definition 'In-situ sensors that simultaneuously measure electrical and magnetic fields.  They are usually moored on the seabed for long periods of time for determination of deep structure through monitoring magnetotelluric currents.  However, some may also be configured to be receivers for active electromagnetic surveys such as CSEM.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L05::EMSR'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/70/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/70/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/70/>;
    dc:modified '2019-09-04T10:01:22'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'FAD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'fish aggregating devices'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Any kind of permanent, semi-permanent or temporary structure designed to attract fishes (specially tunas) and used in ocean purse seine fisheries. FADs can be moored or drifting devices and consist of surface or sub-surface buoys or floats to which underwater ropes, lines or chains can be attached. The most sophisticated type can be equipped with an echo sounder to estimate the biomass under it, a GPS to locate the device, and either a VHF, Immarsat or Iridium connection to periodically send the information to the vessel which owns it.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L05::70'^^xsd:string .
